{"study_accession":"PRJNA928833","secondary_study_accession":"SRP425324","title":"LCLF1.0 fastq-Files","description":"In this study, we investigated ad libitum food intake of 20 healthy adult volunteers who each completed a 4-week stay at the National Institutes of Health (NIH). During their stay, they consumed a low-carbohydrate, high-fat (LCHF) diet and a low-fat, high-carbohydrate (LFHC) diet for 2 weeks each, in random order. We collected information about energy intake and metabolic changes in response to the two test diets. The test diets were presented to subjects in amounts exceeding their daily energy requirements, and subjects were instructed to eat as much or as little of each diet as desired. This study implemented 7-day rotating menus for each test diet. The diets were matched for presented calories and protein, but the LCHF diet was low in carbohydrate (~10% of calories) and high in fat (... (for more see dbGaP study page.)","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":18,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN33330380","study_accession":"PRJNA928833","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Non-tumor RNA sample from Blood of a human female participant in the dbGaP study \"LCLF1.0 Data\"","description":"Non-tumor RNA sample from Blood of a human female participant in the dbGaP study \"LCLF1.0 Data\"","sex":"female","geo_sample":"","access":"controlled","dbgap":"phs003187","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-12-02","attributes":[["gap_accession","phs003187"],["submitter_handle","NIDDK_LCLF"],["biospecimen_repository","NIDDK_LCLF"],["study_name","LCLF1.0 Data"],["study_design","Clinical Trial"],["biospecimen_repository_sample_id","LCLF-006_00"],["submitted_sample_id","LCLF-006_00"],["submitted_subject_id","LCLF-006"],["gap_sample_id","5283883"],["gap_subject_id","4399388"],["sex","female"],["tissue","Blood"],["histological_type","peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["analyte_type","RNA"],["is_tumor","No"],["gap_consent_code","1"],["gap_consent_short_name